sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-01> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Computation is the central organizing idea of the new science" ;
    dct:description "The most important idea underlying Wolfram's new kind of science is computation: systems such as cellular automata should be viewed as computations, with initial conditions as input and later states as output, so that systems with entirely different rules can be discussed in a unified, abstract way." ;
    delphi:context "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Computation as a Framework” (from p. 637), p. 637. Scope: the methodology of the new kind of science; cellular automata and other simple programs" ;
    dct:type "conceptual" .
}

